{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":1512217,"ns":0,"title":"Fin field-effect transistor","extract":"A fin field-effect transistor (FinFET) is a multigate device, a MOSFET (metal–oxide–semiconductor field-effect transistor) built on a substrate where the gate is placed on two, three, or four sides of the channel or wrapped around the channel (gate all around), forming a double or even multi gate structure. These devices have been given the generic name \"FinFETs\" because the source/drain region forms fins on the silicon surface.","description":"Type of non-planar transistor","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}